# CODEOWNERS — coverage model (un-inverted).
#
# DEFAULT = UNOWNED: any path not matched below needs no code-owner review, so a
# low-risk deterministic PR (and a Margot LOW-risk verdict) can merge without the
# operator. There is deliberately NO `* @owner` catch-all — the wiki's knowledge
# content and docs flow unattended.
#
# OWNED (listed below) = the safety / identity / gate machinery: a judgment change
# there must have a human. The branch ruleset requires code-owner review (with 0
# baseline approvals), so touching an owned path holds the PR for @lexijamesesq;
# touching only unowned paths does not.
#
# When adding a path: uncertain -> OWNED (under-coverage — an owned path left
# unowned — is the dangerous direction). Anchored patterns (/path/ or /file) over
# bare names.

# --- Gate machinery (CI/gate/hook chain and its configs) ---
/.github/workflows/            @lexijamesesq
/.github/dependabot.yml        @lexijamesesq
/.pre-commit-config.yaml       @lexijamesesq

# --- Gate/lint configs that can DISABLE a check (gate self-protection) ---
/.gitleaks.toml                @lexijamesesq
/.gitleaks.ci.toml             @lexijamesesq
/.house-code.json              @lexijamesesq
/.house-qa.json                @lexijamesesq

# --- Governance, policy & identity ---
/.claude/settings.json         @lexijamesesq
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @lexijamesesq
/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json   @lexijamesesq
/.claude-plugin/plugin.json    @lexijamesesq

# --- Knowledge-gate machinery (the lint/gatekeeper guarding the vault contract) ---
/.track-list-guard.sh          @lexijamesesq
/.claude/skills/lint-knowledge/lint.py    @lexijamesesq
/.claude/skills/lint-knowledge/tests/     @lexijamesesq
/.claude/skills/gatekeeper/    @lexijamesesq

# --- The knowledge contract / calibration specs (policy) ---
/spec/knowledge-contract.md    @lexijamesesq
/spec/calibration-surface.md   @lexijamesesq
/spec/integration-modes.md     @lexijamesesq

# UNOWNED by default (flow without the operator): README.md, LICENSE, the
